{"cases":[{"attack":true,"case":"SRC_001 names a dependence relation ('depends on SRC_003 by operationalizing the Epistemic Agency probe') but the refutation hook attacks a measurement-validity property of the probe itself (flagged-decoy presence confounded with intelligence), not the dependence link between 0d16ae40c2a5 and SRC_003. No causal mechanism is given for WHY 0d16ae40c2a5 depends on SRC_003 — only that SRC_003 supplies a discriminator. A 'probe supplies a discriminator' is a summary of what SRC_003 contains; the dependence claim needs a stated mechanism (e.g., SRC_003's findings alter the causal path by which 0d16ae40c2a5 distinguishes reliability from compliance), which is absent.","target":"1e3e523d9c28e595984a1d6e0b05d28884d11a70ce3aa70966e776b297bfe65b"},{"attack":false,"case":"SRC_002 specifies a contradiction relation ('contradicts the assumption of simple procedural consistency') and supplies the causal mechanism: reliability requires breaking procedure (rejecting the decoy), so procedural-consistency compliance and reliability are inversely related when a decoy is present. The refutation hook directly targets the proposed mechanism (lowest-variance-compliance panels being most reliable would defeat the claim). This is a substantive, kind-named relation with a falsifying condition, satisfying the problem standard.","target":"a9d87ed10e74afbf966e7ddef84a65d49d6133801cd50508bf4c2136d3e101f9"}]}